    "text": "Suppose that a free profinite product G ∗ H is a free profinite group of finite\nrank. Must G and H be free profinite groups?\n   By (J. Neukirch, Arch. Math., 22, no. 4 (1971), 337–357) this may not be true if\nthe rank of G ∗ H is infinite.                                        O. V. Mel’nikov",
